      "properties": {
        "text": ""
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "OmniCam -> Wan ATI / WanTrackToVideo  (profile: wan_track_native)\n\nBase template: Comfy-Org/workflow_templates\n  video_wan_ati.json\nModel, sampler, shift and CLIP vision settings are unchanged from it.\n\nWHAT CHANGED\nThe hand-drawn trajectory string is gone. Monitor compiles tracks_json from\nthe Director's motion layers, and drives width / height / length so the\ncoordinate space cannot drift out of sync with the generation.\n\nHOW TO USE\n1. In the Director, open Motion Tracks and draw or project a layer.\n   - Draw: click a path over the frame.\n   - Project: pick a 3D object or world point and let the camera project it.\n2. Queue, then read the 'Encodable trajectories' preflight line.\n3. Wire your own start image into WanTrackToVideo.start_image.\n\nWHAT THIS FORMAT CANNOT SAY\nThe JSON marks every supplied point visible and zero-pads the rest, so it\nhas no way to express 'appears later' or 'disappears and returns'. A layer\nhidden on the first sample is dropped; one with a gap is cut at the gap.\nMonitor names the affected layers instead of silently encoding less.\n\nSOURCE GRID\nUpstream pads the JSON to 121 samples and resamples it to the generation\nlength. Monitor emits exactly that grid, spanning the shot's real frame\ntimes, so every generated frame lands on a sample.\n\nMODELS REQUIRED\n  diffusion_models/Wan2_1-I2V-ATI-14B_fp8_e4m3fn.safetensors\n  text_encoders/umt5_xxl_fp8_e4m3fn_scaled.safetensors\n  clip_vision/clip_vision_h.safetensors\n  vae/wan_2.1_vae.safetensors"
      ],
